From 15e35e05ddf3a5c5f930ba48726f2bf62bfd9b57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhymabek Roman <robanokssamit@yandex.ru>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:30:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] twinapi, windows.ui, windows.media, windows.graphics: Answer
 IAgileObject on WinRT activation factories

Every WinRT activation factory handed out by RoGetActivationFactory is an agile
object on Windows: combase marshals the factory pointer into the process that
asked for it and C++/WinRT, CsWinRT and the Windows App SDK CFlat projection all
resolve an agile reference on it (winrt::copy_from / get_agile_reference) before
they use it.  The Wine implementations of these factories listed IUnknown,
IInspectable and IActivationFactory only, so that QueryInterface returned
E_NOINTERFACE for {94ea2b94-e9cc-49e0-c0ff-ee64ca8f5b90} and the caller refused
to use a factory it had just successfully resolved.

WhatsApp Desktop reaches this while it initialises its window: the
Windows.UI.ViewManagement.UISettings and AccessibilitySettings activation
factories (windows.ui.dll) were resolved for the DPI and theme lookup of the
WinUI 3 window, the Windows App SDK asked them for IAgileObject, got
E_NOINTERFACE, and the reference machinery abandoned the object.  The trace
shows exactly four such refusals, all of them
fixme:ui:factory_QueryInterface {94ea2b94-e9cc-49e0-c0ff-ee64ca8f5b90} not
implemented, returning E_NOINTERFACE, immediately around the window activation
path; they are gone after this change.

Audit every activation factory QueryInterface in the tree, not only the ones
that WhatsApp happens to hit: seventeen factories across windows.ui,
windows.graphics, windows.ui.core.textinput, twinapi.appcore,
windows.devices.enumeration, windows.media, windows.media.playback.mediaplayer,
windows.system.profile.systemid, windows.security.authentication.onlineid,
windows.security.credentials.ui.userconsentverifier and appxdeploymentclient
were missing it.  This continues the same rule that patch 0043 established for
the twinapi.appcore and CoreMessaging factories.

The interfaces that stay unimplemented on a factory (the custom marshaler an
agile object does not need, the reference tracker interfaces that must not be
answered, per patch 0043) are still reported through FIXME and answered with
E_NOINTERFACE.

Update the conformance tests that asserted the opposite rule for these
factories.  windows.ui uisettings (82 tests), windows.graphics (9),
twinapi.appcore (137), windows.media (45), windows.system.profile.systemid (26),
windows.ui.core.textinput (35) and windows.media.playback.mediaplayer (20)
all pass; in windows.devices.enumeration the two factory assertions at
devices.c:867 and devices.c:1430 pass and the remaining suite failures are the
pre-existing ones on devices.c:162, 1005, 1014, 1024, 1093, 1148 and 1175,
which come from there being no enumerable devices in this environment.

Signed-off-by: Zhymabek Roman <robanokssamit@yandex.ru>
